    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φευκ-τέον</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must flee,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπό τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					62d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦρο τοῖς κακοῖσι φ.</span>
			they <i>must flee,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Heracl.</u>
				259
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				392
			</span></i> (lyr.): pl., Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.149
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκολασίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					507d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.6.4
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φευκτέος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
			<i>to be avoided,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).850
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>VP</u>
					31.190
				</span></i>
			.</div>
